ents{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pm-tech-user","id":202666680,"login":"pm-tech-user","node_id":"U_kgDODBRyuA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pm-tech-user","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/commit/a36fe82ad240825cf4c14bdf9f53f2ca81f3cc32","node_id":"C_kwDOPhD0vtoAKGEzNmZlODJhZDI0MDgyNWNmNGMxNGJkZjlmNTNmMmNhODFmM2NjMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/commit/f03d43c93205017de87dcfd566c99daa010477bc","sha":"f03d43c93205017de87dcfd566c99daa010477bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/commits/f03d43c93205017de87dcfd566c99daa010477bc"}],"sha":"a36fe82ad240825cf4c14bdf9f53f2ca81f3cc32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/commits/a36fe82ad240825cf4c14bdf9f53f2ca81f3cc32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7794387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/commits/f03d43c93205017de87dcfd566c99daa010477bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:36:46Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:36:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: redirect to error page on 404 and centralize error handling (#637)\n\n## What changed\n\n- `ErrorHandlerService.handleError` now accepts an optional context message and redirects to the error page for both 403 (forbidden / access denied) and 404 (`statusCode === 404`) errors; any other error is shown as an alert with the context message followed by the error details.\n- New public `ErrorHandlerService.redirectToErrorPage(error, replaceHistory)` returns whether a redirect happened; `isUnauthorizedAccess` is now private and the `navigateToErorPage` typo is fixed.\n- `NodeContextProcessingService` redirects to the error page when reading account info fails, keeps browser history when the user is already inside the entity, and holds the pending Luigi navigation so the broken view is not rendered.\n- `AccountInfoService` caches per gateway URL instead of `kcpPath`, and a failed request only evicts its own cache entry.\n- `ResourceService` and `OpenSearchService` no longer show alerts themselves; errors propagate to callers.\n- Detail view, resource table card, search list dynamic page, create resource modal and organization management route their errors through `ErrorHandlerService`, so 403/404 errors redirect and other errors show one alert.\n- Bump `@openmfp/ngx` to 1.8.0 and `@openmfp/portal-ui-lib` to 0.197.1.\n\n## Why\n\nWhen the GraphQL gateway returned `404 (Not Found)` for a missing account, the portal still rendered the view instead of the not-found error page. Errors were also alerted twice: once in the service and again in the component.\n\n## Tests\n\nUpdated and extended specs for the error handler, node context processing, router config, account info, resource service, OpenSearch service and the affected components.\n\n`wc.spec.ts` now registers real standalone test components instead of mocking `@angular/elements`. The Angular unit-test builder runs Vitest with `isolate: false`, so when another spec in the same worker had already loaded the real module, the `vi.mock` was skipped and the tests failed intermittently in CI.\n\n`npm test` passes (lib: 598 tests, wc: 646 tests).\n\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP grzegorz.krajniak@sap.com\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"adb9a02c0976fd25665be7baae6b47900c294542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/git/trees/adb9a02c0976fd25665be7baae6b47900c294542"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/platform-mesh/portal-ui-lib/git/commits/f03d43c93205017de87dcfd566c99daa010477bc","verification":{"payload":"tree adb9a02c0976fd25665be7baae6b47900c294542\nparent faf429fcca4b439c0cf534d20a5ff156ea1db606\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1790858206 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790858206 +0200\n\nfix: redirect to error page on 404 and centralize error handling (#637)\n\n## What changed\n\n- `ErrorHandlerService.handleError` now accepts an optional context message and redirects to the error page for both 403 (forbidden / access denied) and 404 (`statusCode === 404`) errors; any other error is shown as an alert with the context message followed by the error details.\n- New public `ErrorHandlerService.redirectToErrorPage(error, replaceHistory)` returns whether a redirect happened; `isUnauthorizedAccess` is now private and the `navigateToErorPage` typo is fixed.\n- `NodeContextProcessingService` redirects to the error page when reading account info fails, keeps browser history when the user is already inside the entity, and holds the pending Luigi navigation so the broken view is not rendered.\n- `AccountInfoService` caches per gateway URL instead of `kcpPath`, and a failed request only evicts its own cache entry.\n- `ResourceService` and `OpenSearchService` no longer show alerts themselves; errors propagate to callers.\n- Detail view, resource table card, search list dynamic page, create resource modal and organization management route their errors through `ErrorHandlerService`, so 403/404 errors redirect and other errors show one alert.\n- Bump `@openmfp/ngx` to 1.8.0 and `@openmfp/portal-ui-lib` to 0.197.1.\n\n## Why\n\nWhen the GraphQL gateway returned `404 (Not Found)` for a missing account, the portal still rendered the view instead of the not-found error page. Errors were also alerted twice: once in the service and again in the component.\n\n## Tests\n\nUpdated and extended specs for the error handler, node context processing, router config, account info, resource service, OpenSearch service and the affected components.\n\n`wc.spec.ts` now registers real standalone test components instead of mocking `@angular/elements`. The Angular unit-test builder runs Vitest with `isolate: false`, so when another spec in the same worker had already loaded the real module, the `vi.mock` was skipped and the tests failed intermittently in CI.\n\n`npm test` passes (lib: 598 tests, wc: 646 tests).\n\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP grzegorz.krajniak@sap.com\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvlPeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtXEQACirxLBh2FikZrVzfyJ4ikAx\nCx9uyBMStcr8FO7OZENumnVp91F/6nK0YFcUlvSIZ+Zjj9xECbcv+RzZrZK43NDc\n3/6IH9sJ7UfodUPa